# SafeOpsAgent sudoers reference template
# --------------------------------------
# SafeOpsAgent is designed to run as the restricted opsagent user.
# SafeExecutor already enforces a command allowlist, denylist, timeout, and
# structured audit trail. The default deployment does not require sudoers.
#
# Read-only tools should run with normal user privileges whenever possible.
# If an administrator decides to grant additional privileges, review every
# command and every allowed argument according to least privilege principles,
# then install a separately approved sudoers file with visudo.
#
# Risk groups for manual review:
#   Low risk examples:
#     # opsagent ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/id "", /usr/bin/whoami "", /usr/bin/uname -a
#
#   Medium risk examples:
#     # opsagent ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/df -h, /usr/bin/ps aux, /usr/sbin/ss -lntp
#
#   High risk commands:
#     # find, du, journalctl, systemctl
#     # Do not grant broad root NOPASSWD access to these commands by default.
#     # If they are absolutely required, constrain exact arguments manually and
#     # validate the final file with: visudo -c -f /etc/sudoers.d/<file>
#
# This template intentionally contains no active sudo rule.
